<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narasimhadeva I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1238–1264</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narasimhadeva I was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-ganga-dynasty">Eastern Ganga dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, ruling from 1238 to 1264. He took the offensive against the Muslim rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, defeating them in the 1240s and raiding their territory. He is best known as the builder of the Sun Temple at Konark.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narasimhadeva-i.jpg" alt="Narasimhadeva I" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ashok3932 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narasingha_deva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
